course: dictionary
lesson: 7059
title: One word, many meanings: patch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word patch can mean different things, so context tells you which one is meant. «Watch out for patches of ice on the path in winter.» Here a patch is a small area that looks different from the ground around it. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence?
explain: Now read this: «The grass snake, with two yellow patches behind its head, is harmless.» The patches are areas of colour, not pieces of cloth. The word around it, yellow, is the clue.
explain: Patch can also be a verb. When Mum sews a patch on the knee of your jeans, she is patching them. Patch things up is different again: it means to make friends after an argument.
fact: A patch is a small area that looks different from what is around it, such as a wet patch or a patch of ice.
fact: A patch can be a small piece of material sewn over a hole, like the badges sewn on as patches.
fact: A vegetable patch is a small piece of land for growing things, as in «Think of a vegetable patch at school».
fact: To patch things up means to make friends again after an argument.
fact: A rough patch is a hard time, so a person in a rough patch is having a difficult period.
exercise: «Watch out for patches of ice on the path in winter.» What does patch mean here? | A cover worn over one eye | *A small area that looks different from what is around it, like ice | A small area that looks different from what is around it | A sticky pad that gives medicine
exercise: Mum sewed a patch over the hole in Ella's jeans. What is a patch? | A bruise on the knee | A piece of land for growing vegetables | A small update that fixes a computer | *A small piece of material sewn over a hole or worn place
exercise: «That robin will fight other robins to keep its patch.» What does its patch mean? | A quick repair to its nest | A small piece of land it defends | *A small piece of land it defends as its own | A patch of red feathers on its breast
test: «The grass snake, with two yellow patches behind its head, is harmless.» What are the patches? | Pieces of cloth | Sticky medicine pads | Small pieces of land | *Areas of yellow colour
test: Ben and Sam had an argument, but after lunch they patched things up. What does patched things up mean? | They played a game alone | They tore their clothes | *They made friends again | They mended a football
exam: «My brother is in a rough patch at school, but he is patching things up with his friends.» What does rough patch mean? | A bumpy road | A sticky medicine pad | *A rough area of land | A hard time
